<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khalifa bin Harub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1960</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Khalifa II bin Harub</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> bin Harub was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Zanzibar from 1911 to 1960, under the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. Real power lay with the British resident, but during his long reign he was a respected figurehead and symbol of continuity, while the economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a> and the Arab landed elite. He was succeeded by his son Abdullah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khalifa-bin-harub.jpg" alt="Khalifa bin Harub" width="192" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khalifa_bin_Hareb_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
